Subject: [PATCH 07709/11362] [outer-loop] ARC end-to-end gate = honest
 NEGATIVE: detector perception does not yet recover 7/8 (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5834)

Fed detector-produced perception to gemma's goal prompt (same rules as the 5832
oracle ablation). Result: 0 correct, 2 partial, 6 wrong -- far below the oracle's 7/8.
Root causes: (1) the model's own WRONG learned rules dominate the detector's weaker
"ignore this band" note; (2) the detector names the player but not the target;
(3) mover missed on 4/8. The 2 partials (ls20, cn04) are the mover-detected games,
both producing the right shape "move the player to a target".

Lesson: the oracle got 7/8 because it REPLACED the framing; the detector ADDS entities
alongside the wrong rules. Fix must RE-AUTHOR: retract HUD-band rules, name the mover's
target, improve mover recall. This is a sharper, earned target than "add a detector".

